## Setup

```bash
pnpm install
```

## Usage

```bash
pnpm build
pnpm typecheck
pnpm lint
pnpm format
```

Code lives in `src/`, the suite in `tests/`, the generators in `scripts/`.

## Test

```bash
pnpm check
pnpm test
```

`pnpm check` is the whole gate: typecheck, lint, `pnpm test` and `pnpm readme:check`.

## Requirements

`REQUIREMENTS.md` is the standing, numbered requirement set — the contract this project
commits to. New behaviour starts as a requirement diff, then tagged tests, then code; a
row is `implemented` only when a test named in its evidence cell pins it. `pnpm test`
fails when a status and the suite disagree.

`docs/code-map.md` is generated by `scripts/code-map.mjs` from the import graph and each
module's contract header: `pnpm map` rewrites it, `pnpm map:check` fails when it is stale, and
`pnpm map:impact <file...>` prints a change's blast radius (no `--` before the path — pnpm
forwards it literally, unlike npm, so it reads as a bogus module). Coverage and layers are
declared in `code-map.config.json`.

`pnpm readme:check` holds this README to the same standard (G-012): every command, path,
flag and script name here has to exist. `scripts/readme-check.mjs --list` prints what it
checks.

Scaffolded from the nana-pi TypeScript template; `uvx copier update` re-syncs it
when the template evolves. Agent-facing structure and rules live in `AGENTS.md`.
